
                            1oo% UllaGulla v1.0
                        written by Neurodancer/1oo%
                                20-Jun-1999

Introduction.
---------------------------------------------------------------------------
For  every  subdirectory  branch  in  my BBS, I have created separate areas
where files can be uploaded. I move uploaded files to the correct subboards
myself, rather than having my callers search the appropriate directory This
has  the  advantage  that  the  caller  doesn't  need to search the correct
subboard  for  his  upload,  and that I don't end with uploads being in the
wrong subboards.

My Amiga area for example consists of various subboards and subdirectories,
e.g.  for  Demos,  Utilities,  Antivirus programs, Datatypes, etc. etc. The
caller does *not* have upload access in these areas. I also have a subboard
"Amiga  Uploads", and callers do have upload access *only* in this subboard
of the whole set of subboards in the "Amiga" subdirectory.

Now,  if  anyone  tries an upload in any other than the designated "Upload"
subboard,  CNet  will  only tell the caller he/she has no upload access and
leave them alone with that.

Entering  UllaGulla.  If  the  above  happens with UllaGulla installed, the
caller  will  get  a  message  where  the upload should go to, and a prompt
asking  him  if he/she wishes to directly go there and start the upload. OR
UllaGulla  will  take  the  caller  to  the correct subboard automatically,
without any prompt, and invoke the "U" command for him.

UllaGulla  is  a  very  "quiet"  tool,  it won't output much except a small
message  and,  if  configured, the prompt. Its just there to make uploading
easier. The name is just a gaga variation of "UpLoads GO"... :)


